Koala UI License

Copyright (c) 2026 Koala UI. All rights reserved except as granted below.

This license covers the Koala UI component library, design tokens, sections, page examples
and templates ("Koala UI"), however you obtain them: through the koalaui CLI, from this
repository, or by copying them from the documentation. The koalaui CLI itself
(packages/koalaui) is licensed separately under the MIT license in that folder.

Koala UI comes in two tiers:

  Free  Everything installable without a license key: the components in components/ui,
        the helpers in lib, the tokens in registry/koala.css, and the one sample section
        of each section family that the Koala UI website shows with its source.
  Pro   Everything that needs a license key: every other section, the page examples, the
        source of the templates shown as demos on the Koala UI website, and the Figma
        library.


1. WHAT YOU MAY DO

Free tier. You may use, copy and modify the Free tier, at no cost, to build any number of
websites, applications and other end products, for yourself or for clients, commercial or
not, including open-source end products.

Pro tier. Buying a license gives you a perpetual, non-exclusive, non-transferable right to
use, copy and modify the Pro tier to build any number of end products, for yourself or for
clients, commercial or not. There is no subscription: the license does not expire, and it
includes the updates published while Koala UI is offered.

An "end product" is a website, application or other work whose value to its users is more
than Koala UI itself. A client site built with Koala UI is an end product; a template, theme
or UI kit made from Koala UI is not (see section 2).

Seats. A Pro license covers the number of people its plan states: one person for Solo, and
up to six people for Agency. Each person activates their own seat with the koalaui CLI; a
continuous-integration job run for a licensed person may use one of that person's seats.
Unlocking the source on the Koala UI website uses no seat, and is limited to the people the
plan covers. You may not share a license key, or the activation ids issued for it, beyond
the seats you bought.

Third parties. Fonts, photographs and other assets that a template or section loads from
third-party services are licensed by their owners under their own terms, not by this
license.

Clients. You may hand an end product, including its source code, to a client. The client
may keep using and maintaining that end product, but receives no right to use Koala UI in
any other project unless they buy their own license.


2. WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO

For either tier, you may not:

  a. Sell, license, sublicense or give away Koala UI, in whole or in part, as it is or
     modified, other than inside an end product as described above.
  b. Use Koala UI to create a product that competes with it: a component library, UI kit,
     design system, theme, template, page builder or code generator offered to others.
  c. Remove or alter the copyright and license notices in the source files.

For the Pro tier, you also may not:

  d. Publish Pro source where people other than your team and your clients can read it,
     including public code repositories, gists and package registries. An open-source end
     product may use the Free tier, but not the Pro tier.
  e. Share, resell or publish your license key or its activation ids, or use them for more
     seats than you bought.

Pro files carry a comment that identifies the license they were installed with. Removing it
does not change these terms.


3. TERMINATION

If you break these terms, your license ends and you must stop using Koala UI in new work.
End products that you delivered before the license ended, while it was valid, may keep
running. A refunded purchase ends the Pro license the same way.


